- Quantitative effect estimates for included trial(s):
  - From Study 1 abstract:
    - Mortality: HR 0.57 (95% CI 0.43–0.77), p=0.0002.
    - Deaths: 74 (28%) in cotrimoxazole vs 112 (42%) in placebo after median follow-up 19 months.
    - Severe adverse events (grade 3/4): 16 (6%) cotrimoxazole vs 18 (7%) placebo.
    - Severe neutropenia once <0.5×10^9/L: 16 (6%) cotrimoxazole vs 7 (3%) placebo, p=0.06.
    - Subgroup findings: benefits across ages and baseline CD4; persisted beyond 12 months (HR 0.48 [0.27–0.84]).
  - We can derive approximate absolute risk reduction (ARR) and number needed to treat (NNT):
    - ARR ≈ 42% − 28% = 14% over ~19 months.
    - NNT ≈ 1 / 0.14 ≈ 7 (over ~19 months).
- Evidence gaps:
  - No RCTs among infants <18 months born to HIV-infected mothers are evident in the provided set; identify as a gap.

